From 69ab2c932dbd9f7bb14bbfa67528bfc62168d527 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yun Dou <dixyes@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:27:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] arm64: Add emulation of the RCpc acquire loads

A CPU without FEAT_LRCPC takes an undefined instruction exception on the
LDAPR and LDAPUR families, which a binary built for a newer target can
contain. There is no reason to refuse to run it when the load it asks for
can be carried out by hand, so it is: the access is made with the
permissions of the task that faulted, and the exception is not passed on.

The load goes through get_user(), so the address is checked against the
task's own page tables, and a fault the fault handler can resolve is
resolved before any error comes back. A fault that cannot be resolved is
reported against the address the instruction would have used, which is
where the task would have seen it. Later accesses are ordered with
dmb ishld, which is stronger than the RCpc ordering the instruction asks
for.

Only EL0 is handled: the kernel's own RCpc loads are substituted at boot
by the alternatives in rwonce.h, so they never reach this path.

The number of loads carried out is counted, and can be read from
<debugfs>/rcpc_emul/stats.

Assisted-by: dsh:DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash
(cherry picked from commit 072a92d304efef6af3178cd1a88593a2784347b6)
---
